                <pb facs="0764" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg656"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr. Douglass</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 116.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department is gratified to receive your
                    No. 157, of the 27th ultimo, inclosing copies of correspondence, from which it
                    appears that the Haitian Government promises to make an executive measure the
                    proposed law repealing the existing law by which sailing vessels are detained in
                    the ports of Haiti until the duties on their inward cargoes are paid.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
